---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy — Dustbound" description="Dustbound Privacy Policy — app and website.">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-panel">
    <SiteHeader />
    <main class="prose-dust mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-10 md:px-8">
      <h1 class="mb-2 text-3xl font-black text-ink md:text-4xl">Dustbound Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 10 August 2026</p>

      <section class="mb-10 space-y-4 text-muted" data-section="intro">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy describes how <strong class="text-ink">Ingenium Software Engineering</strong>
          (“we”, “us”, or “Ingenium”) handles information in connection with the mobile application
          <strong class="text-ink">Dustbound</strong> (Android package <code class="text-accent">dev.ingeniumsoftware.dustbound</code>)
          and the website at <a href="https://dustbound.app/">https://dustbound.app/</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Dustbound is a local-first companion checklist for tracking Sprite collectible progress. It is an unofficial product.
          Dustbound is not affiliated with, endorsed by, supported by, or connected to Epic Games, Inc., and it does not contain any Fortnite materials.
        </p>
        <p>
          For privacy inquiries, contact <a href="mailto:privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev">privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10 space-y-4 text-muted" data-section="app">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">App</h2>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Summary</h3>
        <p>
          Dustbound stores your checklist progress and preferences on your device only. We do not create user accounts,
          do not upload your progress to our servers, and do not use analytics, advertising, or crash-reporting SDKs.
          The app may download publicly available catalog and events data over the internet so checklists stay up to date.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Information stored on your device</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Checklist progress</strong> — which collectibles you have marked as Collected or Mastered.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Preferences</strong> — optional event timezone override and local Event notification settings.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Content caches</strong> — copies of public catalog and events data used offline or between refreshes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          This on-device data is not transmitted to Ingenium. If Android Backup is enabled, the operating system may include app data in device backups according to your system settings.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Network access and permissions</h3>
        <p>
          Dustbound may use network access to download public catalog and events JSON feeds over HTTPS (for example from hosting provided via GitHub Pages).
          These requests do not include your checklist progress. Hosting providers may incidentally receive technical information such as IP address and User-Agent.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you enable Event reminders, Dustbound requests notification permission so it can schedule reminders on your device. Reminder content stays local.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Information we do not collect (app)</h3>
        <p>
          The app does not require accounts, sync progress to Ingenium, include advertising/analytics/crash SDKs, or collect precise location, contacts, or advertising identifiers for our use.
          Paid downloads are handled by Google Play under Google’s policies.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Retention and deletion (app)</h3>
        <p>
          On-device data is retained until you clear Dustbound’s app data or uninstall the app. There is no account-deletion flow because there are no accounts.
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">Children</h3>
        <p>Dustbound is not directed at children, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children through the app.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10 space-y-4 text-muted" data-section="website">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Website</h2>
        <p>
          The marketing website at dustbound.app may collect <strong class="text-ink">email addresses only</strong> when you submit the interest form,
          so we can notify you about Dustbound early releases / launch. We do not ask for name or phone number on that form.
        </p>
        <p>
          Form submissions are processed by <strong class="text-ink">Formspree</strong> on our behalf. See
          <a href="https://formspree.io/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Formspree’s Privacy Policy</a>.
          We keep emails only for that notification purpose, then delete or stop using them. To request deletion, email
          <a href="mailto:privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev">privacy@ingeniumsoftware.dev</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          The website does not set first-party cookies and does not use analytics. See the
          <a href="/cookies/">Cookie policy</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Visiting the site involves normal web hosting (GitHub Pages and any CDN in front), which may process technical connection data such as IP address.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mb-10 space-y-4 text-muted">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink">Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The “Last updated” date will change when we do.
          The current version remains available at <a href="https://dustbound.app/privacy/">https://dustbound.app/privacy/</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="text-sm text-muted">
        Dustbound is an unofficial fan companion. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by, supported by, or connected to Epic Games, Inc.
      </p>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>
